      "writtenOn": "2023-05-09T06:58:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Consider SkPathPriv::Iterate. It provides a much barer-bones representation of the underlying path content whereas SkPath::Iter has lots of extra closing and compacting logic (unless vello requires that to be done here).\n\u003e \n\nDone. I was already disabling `forceClose` above since I enable Vello\u0027s own similar logic in the cxx bridge crate. The compaction logic sounds useful though, I\u0027m not sure if vello implements the same.\n\nWhile at it I fixed the code for conics by approximating them as 2 quads. The vello path representation doesn\u0027t support conics and the previous version of this code was incorrect.\n\n\u003e In the long-long term this won\u0027t matter since that sort of cleanup can happen when SkPathBuilder finishes an SkPath.\n\nThat sounds good to me.",
      "parentUuid": "ecb52efa_b5dfdb11",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 114,
